# Track ONLY the recipes and provenance notes — never the data itself.
# Data is large, often license-restricted, and fully re-buildable with `make`,
# so it lives off in scratch (see common.mk) and is never committed.

# Ignore everything by default …
*
# … except the directory structure and the files that describe how to rebuild it.
!*/
!.gitignore
!*.mk
!Makefile
!*.md
